# Ars Magica Fifth Edition — Example: Darius of Flambeau (Lore)

**Version:** 0.4
**Source:** Ars Magica Fifth Edition (Atlas Games, 2004)
**Publisher:** Atlas Games

> Chapter Three's worked character-creation example: the narrative walkthrough, verbatim. His stat block is converted as a TEMPLATE in arm5e-0.4-character-templates.ttrpg, where the free-with-House Virtue and each Flaw's specifics are structured fields rather than prose.

---

### Example: Darius of Flambeau

Darius starts with the normal Confidence Score of 1 and 3 Confidence Points. His only noteworthy piece of equipment is his talisman-spear; Niall can assume that Darius has any mundane material he needs.

With the statistics completed, Niall finishes filling in the details of Darius’s appearance and background, preparing him for play in the saga.

